-- title:
--   Error bound for the segmented inverse of the resampling system (complex form)
-- statement:
--   Let $s\le t$ be lengths with $s>0$, let $\alpha\ge 2$ be the Gaussian parameter and assume $x=\alpha^2\theta=\alpha^2(t-s)/s\ge 3$ (`xθ s t α`). Let $B$ be a valid block structure (`BlocksOK s t B`: wrap-free runs partitioning $[0,s)$ with coupling width $w=B.w$) whose blocks all have length at most $\lambda$, and let $T$ be precomputed fixed-point tables of precision $P$ accurate to $E\ge 0$ ulps with per-block constants bounded by $D_m$ (`TabOK P s t α B T E Dm`). Put $G=D_m\,((\lambda+1)E+1)\,(B_u+1)\,(\lambda+1)\,(2w+1)\,(|J|+1)^2$ (`segG`), where $|J|$ is the number of near-boundary positions of the block structure. Let $U:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z\times\mathbb Z$ be a fixed-point complex input whose real and imaginary parts satisfy $|U_i^{re}/2^P|,|U_i^{im}/2^P|\le B_u$ ($B_u\ge 0$), and let $v,w:\mathbb N\to\mathbb C$ satisfy $\|w_i\|\le W_m$, the system $w_i+(E w)_i=v_i$ with the exact coupling operator `Eexact s t α` for $i<s$, and $|U_i^{re}/2^P-\operatorname{Re}v_i|\le\varepsilon_{in}$, $|U_i^{im}/2^P-\operatorname{Im}v_i|\le\varepsilon_{in}$. Write $\delta=\frac{60G}{2^P}+3\cdot4e^{-\pi\alpha^2w(w+1)}(B_u+1)+\frac87\varepsilon_{in}$. If $1000\,G\le2^P$, then for every $i<s$ the complex segmented inverse `segInvC P T B U` has real and imaginary parts each within $\delta$ of $\operatorname{Re}w_i$, $\operatorname{Im}w_i$, and $\|\mathrm{segInvC}(U)_i/2^P-w_i\|\le 2\delta$ (as a complex number via `toC`).
